  "note": "Trademarks and public figures. Both are RESTRICTED rather than BLOCKED: parody, commentary and nominative use are real, and a coin called after a famous person is not automatically fraud. What they forbid is PAID MEDIA without a human review, because the operator buying advertising for a coin trading on someone else's mark is the operator participating in the infringement. `requireBoundary` is mandatory on short marks - `nike` inside `unikernel`, `venue` inside `response` - and stating it explicitly is what stops a five-letter mark from quietly flagging a tenth of the corpus. This file is ADDITIVE to DEFAULT_LEXICON in packages/screening/src/lexicon.ts and deliberately does not repeat what that file already carries.",
